                        "review": "Amazing game! I think this the only metroidvania I've played that doesn't have traditional combat. You go around and learn about the wildlife, by taking pictures, and learning how to deal with each of them. In the beginning it's a lot of distraction and run. As you progress you learn different ways to deal with each creature. Each encounter is like a mini puzzle with different ways to handle them. \n\nIf you like metroidvanias and are willing to try something new, I would give it a shot.",
